# readline — real-world examples

Keyboard shortcuts for bash/zsh and anything else built on GNU Readline.

## Moving around

| Keys | Action |
|------|--------|
| `Ctrl-b` / `Ctrl-f` | Move one character left / right |
| `Alt-b` / `Alt-f` | Move one word left / right |
| `Ctrl-a` / `Ctrl-e` | Jump to start / end of line |
| `Ctrl-x x` | Jump to start, then back to end |

## Cut, copy and paste

| Keys | Action |
|------|--------|
| `Backspace` / `DEL` | Delete character left of cursor |
| `Ctrl-d` | Delete character under cursor |
| `Ctrl-u` | Kill from cursor back to line start |
| `Ctrl-k` | Kill from cursor to end of line |
| `Alt-d` | Kill word forward |
| `Ctrl-w` | Kill word backward |
| `Ctrl-y` | Yank (paste) last killed text |
| `Alt-y` | Cycle to previously killed text after Ctrl-y |

## History

| Keys | Action |
|------|--------|
| `Ctrl-p` / `Ctrl-n` | Previous / next history line |
| `Alt->` | Jump to the line currently being entered |
| `Ctrl-r` / `Ctrl-s` | Incremental search backward / forward |
| `Ctrl-j` | End an incremental search |
| `Ctrl-g` | Abort search, restore original line |
| `Alt-Ctrl-y` | Yank first argument of previous command |
| `Alt-.` or `Alt-_` | Yank LAST argument of previous command |

## Undo and screen

| Keys | Action |
|------|--------|
| `Ctrl-_` or `Ctrl-x Ctrl-u` | Undo last edit (repeatable) |
| `Alt-r` | Revert all changes to this line |
| `Ctrl-l` | Clear screen, reprint current line |

## Completion

| Keys | Action |
|------|--------|
| `TAB` | Auto-complete a name |
| `Alt-/` | Filename completion (no smart completion) |
| `Alt-?` | List possible completions |
| `Alt-*` | Insert all possible completions |

## Transpose

| Keys | Action |
|------|--------|
| `Ctrl-t` | Drag character before cursor over the one at cursor |
| `Alt-t` | Drag word before cursor over the following word |

## Everyday combos on the homelab

```sh
# Re-run last command's file argument with a new command:
less /var/log/zypper.log
wc -l Alt-.          # expands to: wc -l /var/log/zypper.log

# Fix a typo at line start without retyping:
# Ctrl-a, fix it, Ctrl-e to return

# Recall that long zypper command from yesterday:
# Ctrl-r then type "zypper dup"
```

```sh
# Make readline vi-style instead (in ~/.inputrc)
set editing-mode vi
```
